<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<div class="wrap narrow">
  <p class="eyebrow">VentureOS</p>
  <h1>Privacy <em>policy</em></h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated 19 November 2026</p>
  <div class="card legal">
    <p>VentureOS (ventureos.africa) is run by <b><%= config.org.name %></b>, part of ScaleGate, <%= config.org.address %>. This policy explains what we collect when you use VentureOS, why, and your rights. We follow the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, and the EU General Data Protection Regulation where it applies to you.</p>

    <h3>What we collect</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Your account:</b> your name, email address and, if you give it, your phone number. If you sign in with Google, Google tells us only your name, email address and that the email is confirmed. We never receive your Google password.</li>
      <li><b>Your applications:</b> what you tell us about your venture, team, finances and plans, and the documents you upload.</li>
      <li><b>Meetings, messages and events:</b> meeting invitations and replies, messages with our team, and event registrations.</li>
      <li><b>Technical records:</b> a sign-in cookie that keeps you signed in, and records of actions on your application (for example when it was sent or a document opened), kept for security and so we can answer questions about what happened.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Why we use it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>To create your account and sign you in.</li>
      <li>To review your application, arrange meetings and write to you about it.</li>
      <li>To decide, with ScaleGate's partners and committee, whether and how we can work with you. People make every decision; software only helps prepare it.</li>
      <li>To run events you register for.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We use your information because you ask us to consider your application (taking steps before a possible agreement), and for our legitimate interest in running a fair and secure selection process. We do not sell your information and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

    <h3>Who sees it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>ScaleGate staff, reviewers and committee members working on your application. Reviewers must declare any conflict of interest before they can read it.</li>
      <li>Service providers who help us run VentureOS (our server in Lagos and our email service), only to provide that service.</li>
      <li>Investors, partners or programme sponsors only with your permission, or as part of a programme you have agreed to join.</li>
      <li>Authorities where the law requires it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where it is kept and for how long</h3>
    <p>VentureOS and its files are stored on a server in Lagos, Nigeria. We keep application records for as long as we are considering or working with you, and then for up to six years so we can answer questions and meet legal duties, unless you ask us to delete them sooner and the law allows it.</p>

    <h3>Your rights</h3>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your information, to object to how we use it, or to receive a copy. Write to <a href="mailto:<%= config.org.email %>"><%= config.org.email %></a>. You may also complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (ndpc.gov.ng) or, in the EU, to your local data protection authority.</p>

    <h3>Google sign-in</h3>
    <p>If you choose <b>Continue with Google</b>, we use the information Google gives us (name, email address and that it is confirmed) only to sign you in to VentureOS and to address you by name. Our use of information received from Google APIs follows the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>

    <h3>Changes and contact</h3>
    <p>We will post any change to this policy here. Questions: <a href="mailto:<%= config.org.email %>"><%= config.org.email %></a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
